WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:10.777
Welcome back, everyone it's Charlie

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:13.146
This will be my Full
Last of Us Episode 7 Video.

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:15.448
There were a whole bunch of Easter eggs
and references to the game,

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:17.884
so we'll break it all down
if you're brand new to the channel.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:20.120
Be sure to subscribe
to get all the episodes

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.123
and careful for spoilers of the episode
if you haven't seen it yet.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.157
We'll start at the beginning.

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:27.260
Work our way through, shot by shot,
talking about Easter eggs and WTF moments,

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:29.462
starting with the title left Behind.

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:32.599
It's a reference to the DLC
from the first game that explains Ellie's

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:33.133
backstory.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:37.137
It's primarily focused on Ellie and Riley,
but just like you saw in the episode,

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:39.539
it jumps back and forth
between the present day

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:42.242
when she's trying to take care of Joel
to keep him from bleeding out

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:43.843
and back in her past.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:47.447
Primarily, it's focused on the events of
their adventure in the abandoned shopping

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:50.550
mall in the Boston Quarantine zone
and the events of Riley's death

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.686
that wound up traumatizing
Ellie even more than she already was.

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:56.456
But the way they end the episode
on the cliffhanger there,

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:59.159
they don't actually show you
what happens to Riley after that.

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:02.195
Like, they end on a bit of a cliffhanger
with her back in present day

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.163
trying to fix Joe.

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:05.465
So we don't know if that's the last time
we've ever seen Riley

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:07.867
or if they'll cover the rest of that
in a future episode,

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.302
because there's still more flashbacks

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:11.438
that we haven't seen yet
that were in the early trailers.

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:15.642
The actual opening scene picks up in
present day in the snowy suburbs nearby

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:18.778
just after the end of Episode six,
with Ellie having drugged Joel

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:19.779
to an abandoned house.

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:21.815
You can see the horse in there
in the house with her,

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:24.117
which is smart of her to do
because it'll keep the Raiders

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:26.653
that attack them from spotting them,
and it'll keep the horse

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:28.988
from wandering off
while she's dealing with Joel.

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:31.391
But he has lost a ton of blood.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.693
He's on the edge of death.
Like you see him breathing.

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:37.163
They want to let you know that
he's still alive, but he's barely alive.

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:39.165
He tries to get her to leave him behind

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:41.101
and return to Tommy's
settlement in the north.

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:43.403
That's what he whispers her.
Go north to Tommy.

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:46.606
They do plan on going back eventually,
but that was meant to be after

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.608
their current mission
of finding the fireflies.

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:49.442
Like Joel did

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:53.213
tell Tommy that he planned to come back
and make a home at his settlement.

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:56.015
And even though they haven't
had that literal conversation yet, like,

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:58.251
what is the future
hold for the two of us together?

00:01:58.251 --> 00:01:59.352
Is a relationship.

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:01.287
Like, are we going to live together
in a household

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.189
or are we going to make a family together?

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.558
When they came back together
at the end of last week's episode,

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:09.395
they kind of implied that they had sort of
to think of each other more closely

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:11.297
and they would probably head
in that direction.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.666
But they haven't
literally said that to each other yet

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.768
in the way they edited
this part of the episode,

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:18.271
the way she puts her
hand on the door to leave the room.

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.206
If you haven't played the video game
before,

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:23.243
they kind of want you to think
she might actually leave him behind

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.712
because the title of the episode
is left Behind.

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:29.249
But as we find, it's
more of a reference to Riley's character.

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:31.017
Really,
though, she's just leaving the room

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:32.952
to look for more supplies
to close his wound,

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:35.221
which he doesn't find
till the end of the episode.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:38.024
Then they flash back to the events
before episode one.

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:39.325
It's not that long ago,

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:42.362
within a year or so of episode one,
maybe a little bit less than that.

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:44.697
The music track
they pick up on is a super deep cut.

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:47.800
It's Pearl Jam's all for none,
and it's meant to be a metaphor

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:50.270
for Ellie's current life in the Boston
Quarantine zone.

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.571
Life is hopeless for her.

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:54.207
Like the lyrics in the song
say it's the apocalypse.

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:57.143
Humanity is fighting a losing battle
and most have given up

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:59.679
and are just wasting away,
just going through the motions.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:03.516
She has no real prospects other than
becoming part of the fedra system.

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:05.752
The school she's in
is controlled by Phaedra.

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:09.189
It's used as a glorified training program
for new fedra soldiers.

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:12.058
The funny thing
is, Marlene told her in episode one, I'm

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:15.061
the one that put you
in that bedroom school to keep you safe,

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:17.597
not because she wanted her
to become part of Phaedra,

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:19.766
but because she knew
that would be the safest place for her.

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:21.134
But the whole idea with this

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:24.137
fedra school is that they have these
in all the different quarantine zones,

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:25.638
and they use it as a glorified training

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:28.641
program for new fedra soldiers
because their current soldiers

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:32.178
keep dying off
either to fights, accidents or the fungus.

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:33.279
So they need new blood.

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:35.582
They need fresh meat for the grinder,
so to speak.

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:40.320
So any new kids born in the quarantine
zone usually get thrown into the system

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:42.722
or they explain
they wind up becoming bottom feeders,

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:47.026
basically doing these really menial tasks,
really crappy jobs for crappy rations.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.495
Life in general
is meant to be terrible for everyone,

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:53.032
but even more terrible for people
who aren't working for Phaedra.

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:55.902
At this point in the timeline,
Ellie doesn't know she's immune.

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:59.105
That doesn't happen until way later
when they get attacked by the stalker

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:01.741
and she doesn't wind up
turning like a normal person.

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:03.843
And they didn't
even show that in this episode.

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:06.579
So I wonder if there's going to be a part
two to these flashbacks.

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:07.447
We'll see.

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:08.314
At this point, though,

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:11.851
she just thinks she's like every other
normal kid living in the quarantine zone.

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:14.320
The girl who hazes her
during their gym class

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:17.190
for running too slow
isn't supposed to be Abby from the games.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:21.094
The episode credits her as Bethany,
who's meant to be a random foil for Ellie.

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:24.831
Abby is a huge antagonist,
but it's during the Last of Us 2 game,

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:28.368
so the show will have to introduce her in
season two or season three at some point.

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:32.372
She was the daughter of the lead doctor
of the Fireflies in Salt Lake City, Utah.

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:35.642
During the events of the first game,
which they are doing for season one.

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:38.878
So we'll probably meet him
at the end of season one,

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:41.814
but I'm not expecting to meet Abby
at least until season two.

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:43.950
They might reference her
at the end of the season, though.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.352
There are a bunch of references
to the second game

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:49.489
which they'll cover in season
two during episode six.

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:52.158
So even this early on the show,
they're already referencing stuff

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:53.960
from season two and season three.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:57.463
Ellie's friend that the girl references
is Riley, obviously who's disappeared

00:04:57.463 --> 00:05:00.366
because she's dropped out of the
v school and joined the Fireflies.

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:02.101
But Ellie doesn't learn that until later

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:04.570
when Riley returns
after being gone for a little while.

00:05:05.038 --> 00:05:07.874
Her whole thing about fighting back
is meant to show you the anger

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:11.878
that she keeps inside her that starts
to manifest more when she's with Joel.

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:14.147
A really good example of
that is when they first encounter

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:15.348
the hunters in Kansas City.

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:18.618
And she has to save Joel
when she's got her gun on the hunter.

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:21.387
You look at the excitement on her eyes
that flashes for a second

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:22.655
before she gets really scared.

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:25.658
That's her feeding off of the crazy energy
and the violence here.

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:27.960
The showrunner, Neil Druckmann,
talked about this, too.

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:30.763
She's got this violence inside her
that's meant to be kind of

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:34.100
like Joel's violent tendencies,
especially the way Joel was in the past,

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:34.901
the terrible stuff

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:37.103
that Tommy said they did
while they were with the hunters

00:05:37.103 --> 00:05:39.639
before arriving in the Boston
Quarantine zone.

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:40.707
So once Ellie left

00:05:40.707 --> 00:05:43.710
at the beginning of the season with Joel,
they start running into these dangerous

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:46.846
groups and situations
and things get really violent really fast.

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:49.449
It starts to excite her
more like the two of them.

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:52.051
Ellie and Joel need each other
metaphorically and literally,

00:05:52.085 --> 00:05:53.820
because she doesn't quite have the skills

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:56.789
needed to survive a journey across
the United States by herself yet.

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:58.825
She's getting a little bit better.
She got a little bit better.

00:05:58.825 --> 00:06:02.195
Last week's episode in Joel, for example,
needs her to help him

00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:06.099
survive literally this near fatal wound
or save him from the hunters.

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:08.634
And they also need each other's
emotional support.

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:09.302
Like they show you.

00:06:09.302 --> 00:06:10.903
Joel growing as a person,

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:14.907
like becoming more of a person,
so to speak, feeling all the feelings.

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:16.776
So while they have all that positive

00:06:16.776 --> 00:06:20.680
father daughter relationship stuff
developing on the negative side of that,

00:06:20.813 --> 00:06:24.717
both of them kind of feed off of each
other's violence in a toxic kind of way.

00:06:24.751 --> 00:06:27.220
Like just being with Joel
didn't make her more violent.

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:29.489
She already had that in her,
and they kind of

00:06:29.489 --> 00:06:32.191
bring that out of each other
a little bit in situations like this.

00:06:32.525 --> 00:06:33.993
She gets hold of the fedra office

00:06:33.993 --> 00:06:37.530
and the picture of his wife and daughter
remind her of how alone she is.

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:39.499
It's meant to be a metaphor
for the end of the episode

00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:41.801
when she thinks that Riley
is going to abandon her.

00:06:42.135 --> 00:06:44.404
Remember,
the title of the episode is Left Behind.

00:06:44.404 --> 00:06:47.607
It's all about being left behind
or leaving things behind.

00:06:48.007 --> 00:06:50.676
The reveal Ellie's been in the hole
at least three times.

00:06:50.676 --> 00:06:52.111
Remember, this is the apocalypse.

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:54.414
She's only about 13 years old
when this is happening.

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:56.682
Because you didn't start out with Joel
till she's about 14.

00:06:56.849 --> 00:06:59.752
So it's a good picture of just
how bad society has gotten in general,

00:06:59.786 --> 00:07:02.889
putting a 13 year old
in solitary confinement prison style.

00:07:03.256 --> 00:07:04.891
When he gets real with her
about her future

00:07:04.891 --> 00:07:07.193
prospects, it's
either become part of the fedra system,

00:07:07.193 --> 00:07:10.630
become an agent, or live a life similar
to one of the randos

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:13.866
that you saw in episode one, like what
Joel was doing, those random jobs.

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:16.335
Now, obviously,
Joel had a lot of stuff going on inside.

00:07:16.335 --> 00:07:19.472
He's a smuggler with Tess,
but all the regular jobs that he was

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:23.509
pulling on the side just looked total crap
the way he's trying to sell her on it.

00:07:23.543 --> 00:07:27.780
He's basically saying your life could be
slightly less crap or totally crap.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.482
Those are your two options.

00:07:29.482 --> 00:07:31.250
How much crap do you actually want?

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:34.320
Wish you could also make a reference
to Riley later in the episode

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:38.257
when she says she literally was given
the job of managing sewage

00:07:38.257 --> 00:07:39.392
in the Boston Quarantine.

00:07:39.392 --> 00:07:42.829
So like, literally managing
the crap of the Boston Quarantine zone.

00:07:43.162 --> 00:07:45.832
He references the fireflies
catching a bullet from one of them.

00:07:45.865 --> 00:07:49.068
That's because they're super militant,
which they show you later in the episode

00:07:49.068 --> 00:07:51.571
because Riley has been constructing
pipe bombs for them.

00:07:51.871 --> 00:07:55.074
They go after fedra all the time,
and you saw that a little bit in episode

00:07:55.074 --> 00:07:58.811
one when Marlene was planning on breaking
Ellie out at the beginning of the season.

00:07:58.945 --> 00:08:01.013
They plan a massive diversion.

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:03.082
Normally,
they take more guerrilla tactics,

00:08:03.082 --> 00:08:05.585
more isolated incidents like blowing up
cars.

00:08:05.618 --> 00:08:07.720
You saw where Tess was being held.

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:09.822
They do stuff like that all the time.

00:08:09.822 --> 00:08:11.524
They also try to use this conversation

00:08:11.524 --> 00:08:13.926
with the fedra agent
to get you to sympathize more with them,

00:08:14.093 --> 00:08:16.329
because not all of them
are meant to be total dirtbags.

00:08:16.329 --> 00:08:18.798
Like some of them are trying
to hold humanity together.

00:08:18.798 --> 00:08:20.500
Although the way Riley tells it,

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:24.003
the agent here,
this agent wanted her on crap detail.

00:08:24.303 --> 00:08:26.072
So he is a little bit of a dirtbag.

00:08:26.072 --> 00:08:29.242
When he tells Ellie one day she could be
a leader, he sees potential in her.

00:08:29.275 --> 00:08:32.612
That's foreshadowing for present day
when she actually does have to take charge

00:08:32.612 --> 00:08:33.579
and save Joel.

00:08:33.579 --> 00:08:36.983
Also foreshadowing for much later
like beyond the events of the games

00:08:37.049 --> 00:08:39.952
when she could potentially become
a bigger leader to the survivors.

00:08:40.286 --> 00:08:42.488
We'll see if they make the Last of Us
three game.

00:08:42.488 --> 00:08:46.158
Maybe they'll cover some of that
during that game inside her bedroom

00:08:46.158 --> 00:08:48.327
while they're panning across the walls,
all of her stuff.

00:08:48.361 --> 00:08:50.229
The camera lingers on a baseball bat

00:08:50.229 --> 00:08:53.499
that made me think of the infamous
baseball bat from the Last of Us 2.

00:08:53.499 --> 00:08:56.102
I won't say more about that
because it gets into huge spoilers.

00:08:56.102 --> 00:08:59.105
So if you have played the games,
please don't post spoilers for that

00:08:59.105 --> 00:09:00.273
in the comments.

00:09:00.273 --> 00:09:02.708
The dinosaur on her wall
is an Easter egg for the dinosaurs.

00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:03.776
As Joel shows Ellie

00:09:03.776 --> 00:09:06.812
in a museum that they pass through,
which is also in the second game.

00:09:06.812 --> 00:09:09.248
And there are several more mentions
of dinosaurs.

00:09:09.248 --> 00:09:12.752
Later in the episode too,
we see her Will Livingston Book of Puns,

00:09:12.752 --> 00:09:15.488
but it's Volume one,
not the one that she has later.

00:09:15.721 --> 00:09:19.759
That's volume two, and it's given to her
by Riley as a gift later, which we saw

00:09:19.759 --> 00:09:22.795
in the future in previous episodes
when she's reading to Joel.

00:09:23.162 --> 00:09:26.132
The camera also lingers
on her pocketknife, which she winds up

00:09:26.132 --> 00:09:28.868
using later to kill the stalker
at the end of the episode.

00:09:29.201 --> 00:09:31.537
Like, this is going to come in real handy
real soon.

00:09:31.871 --> 00:09:34.140
She's reading one of her Savage
Starlight comic books,

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:36.943
which they've referenced several times
in the Henry and Sam episode.

00:09:36.943 --> 00:09:37.777
R.I.P.

00:09:37.777 --> 00:09:40.780
The actual plot of the Savage
Starlight Comics are usually meant

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:42.882
to be metaphors
for Ellie and Joel's adventures.

00:09:43.082 --> 00:09:46.118
But in this context, for this episode,
it's more of a metaphor for Ellie

00:09:46.118 --> 00:09:48.754
and Riley's adventure together,
because she hasn't met Joel yet.

00:09:48.854 --> 00:09:52.491
And in the comic book issue, they talk
about breaking into this secret area.

00:09:52.525 --> 00:09:55.528
That's what they do in the episode,
breaking in to the abandoned mall.

00:09:55.828 --> 00:09:57.597
There are a couple of movie posters
on her wall.

00:09:57.597 --> 00:10:00.900
There's a Red Planet movie poster
and one for the Lunar Phases of the Moon,

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:04.370
which is a reference to her wish
to travel to the moon, become an astronaut

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:07.173
someday, like her hero, Sally Ride,
which she just told the joke.

00:10:07.406 --> 00:10:09.275
The poster behind her is for Innerspace,

00:10:09.275 --> 00:10:12.411
which is about a group of characters
shrinking down Ant-Man, Dalek.

00:10:12.411 --> 00:10:15.348
Like we just got Ant-Man, the WASP
Quantumania in the movie theaters.

00:10:15.581 --> 00:10:17.316
Inside that movie,
they do something similar.

00:10:17.316 --> 00:10:19.986
They shrink down to go into someone's
body to save them,

00:10:19.986 --> 00:10:22.622
which is also meant to be a reference
to her immunity.

00:10:22.655 --> 00:10:25.591
Her condition
in saving Joel's life in present day.

00:10:25.891 --> 00:10:29.462
You also remember that
culture in the world froze in 2003

00:10:29.462 --> 00:10:32.665
so there wouldn't be any movie posters
or pop culture from after that.

00:10:33.032 --> 00:10:36.736
The empty bed used to be Riley's before
she dropped out and joined the Fireflies.

00:10:36.969 --> 00:10:39.839
She's got a couple old cassette
tapes for her Walkman, AHA's

00:10:39.872 --> 00:10:42.141
Greatest Hits,
which they play later in the episode.

00:10:42.174 --> 00:10:43.743
Also, the Etta James tape.

00:10:43.743 --> 00:10:45.277
I can't see the name of the middle one,

